---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = "Condo Loans in Miami | Mortgage Broker Miami Florida";
const description = "Miami condo mortgage guidance for warrantable, non-warrantable, FHA, conventional, jumbo, investment, and foreign national condo financing.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
<main id="main"><section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Miami condo financing</p><h1>Condo Loans in Miami</h1><p>Miami condo mortgage guidance for warrantable, non-warrantable, FHA, conventional, jumbo, investment, and foreign national condo financing.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Mortgage Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="get-preapproved-miami.html">Get Preapproved</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Calculate Payment</a></div><div class="trust-row"><span class="trust-pill">Matthew Gromadzki</span><span class="trust-pill">NMLS #2560919</span><span class="trust-pill">Miami · Florida</span></div></div><form class="lead-form"><h2>Request a Condo Loans Miami Quote</h2><p>Answer a few basics and we’ll review the best mortgage path for your scenario.</p><label>Loan goal<select><option>Select one</option><option>Buying a home</option><option>Refinancing</option><option>Condo financing</option></select></label><div class="form-row"><label>Purchase price / value<input placeholder="$650,000"></label><label>Down payment / equity<input placeholder="$100,000"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Credit score range<select><option>Select range</option><option>760+</option><option>720–759</option><option>680–719</option><option>640–679</option></select></label><label>Property city<input placeholder="Miami"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Name<input></label><label>Phone<input></label></div><label>Email<input type="email"></label><button class="btn btn-primary full" type="button">Start Mortgage Review</button></form></div></section><section class="section "><div class="container two-col"><article class="prose"><h2>Warrantable vs non-warrantable condos</h2><p>A warrantable condo is generally easier to finance through standard conventional channels. A non-warrantable condo may need a specialized lender, larger down payment, different pricing, or alternative documentation.</p><h2>What lenders may review</h2><p>Lenders may request a condo questionnaire, master insurance certificate, association budget, reserve information, litigation details, assessment information and rental-use rules.</p><h2>How to avoid condo loan surprises</h2><p>Send the building name, address, HOA dues, listing link, occupancy goal, down payment and offer timeline before relying on a quote.</p><ul class="check-grid"><li>Payment estimate</li><li>Cash to close</li><li>Property review</li><li>Documentation checklist</li></ul></article><aside><div class="content-card"><h2>Related loan pages</h2><ul><li><a href="mortgage-broker-miami.html">Mortgage Broker Miami</a></li><li><a href="get-preapproved-miami.html">Get Preapproved</a></li><li><a href="miami-mortgage-rates.html">Mortgage Rates</a></li><li><a href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Calculator</a></li></ul></div></aside></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Can I get a personalized quote?</summary><p>Yes. Send property type, price/value, down payment/equity, credit range, city, occupancy and income type.</p></details><details><summary>Is approval guaranteed?</summary><p>No. Final approval depends on underwriting, documentation, property review and lender guidelines.</p></details><details><summary>Should I start before making an offer?</summary><p>Yes. Miami property type and condo/building review can affect the loan path before contract deadlines.</p></details></div></div></section></main>
</BaseLayout>
